## Research

- **Custody quotes (RQ-01), done:** I second-transcribed the Jay Shetty audio locally. "Abandoned as a child by my own mother" and "like life repeating itself" match the captions word for word, so both stay as quotations.
- **Other strings checked against their pages:** the People Mother's Day lines, the AP rehearsal caption and the 1985 Time passage.
- **Still open behind safe defaults:** nobody has viewed the Truth or Dare graveside scene (RQ-02), and the bell hooks essay has not been read in print (RQ-03). The draft no longer depends on either.

## Your call

- **"Good friends with my son":** in the same Shetty passage she says "I'm really good friends with my son" (audio-confirmed). I left it out because the synthesis says to add nothing about Rocco, so the custody paragraph still ends on her sobbing in the dressing room. One clause would add her own ending.
- **"But it's not enough":** the one optional item worth doing (Rolling Stone 1991, beside "no win stays won") did not fit. It costs about 25 words and needs a matching cut.

